<title>GERMANY: GOLF-LEADING EUROPEAN TOUR MONEY WINNERS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADING EUROPEAN TOUR MONEY WINNERS.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ross McFarlane goes</p>
<p>straight into the European Tour prize-money winners' top 20 in</p>
<p>seventh place following his victory in the European Tournament</p>
<p>Players' Championship on Sunday.</p>
<p>Fellow Briton Ian Woosnam maintains his clear lead over</p>
<p>Germany's Berhard Langer at the head of the list.</p>
<p>Leaders (British unless stated):</p>
<p>  1. Ian Woosnam			     369,793 pounds sterling</p>
<p>  2. Bernhard Langer (Germany)	   256,481</p>
<p>  3. Ernie Els (South Africa)	    239,041</p>
<p>  4. Darren Clarke			   202,713</p>
<p>  5. Miguel Angel Martin (Spain)	 173,026</p>
<p>  6. Jose Maria Olazabal (Spain)	 166,360</p>
<p>  7. Ross McFarlane			  143,901</p>
<p>  8. Lee Westwood			    143,279</p>
<p>  9. Per-Ulrik Johansson (Sweden)	134,825</p>
<p> 10. Mark James				129,383</p>
<p> 11. Richard Green (Australia)	   127,442</p>
<p> 12. Paul Broadhurst			 111,907</p>
<p> 13. Nick Faldo				111,736</p>
<p> 14. Dennis Edlund (Sweden)		110,856</p>
<p> 15. Eduardo Romero (Argentina)	  106,111</p>
<p> 16. Padraig Harrington (Ireland)	100,119</p>
<p> 17. Clinton Whitelaw (South Africa)    98,308</p>
<p> 18. Roger Chapman			    94,829</p>
<p> 19. Peter Mitchell			   94,562</p>
<p> 20. Colin Montgomerie			93,428</p>
